# The one copairing of the sum `Fit | Failed`: `describe` takes it and tests it once; each arm gives back an object
# literal of the interface Report, which its return type names, so each arm builds a Report (`return { .. }`), and the
# route gives the Report either arm built. The early return is the one arm, what follows it the other.

route fits.report.describe
choice describe/?1
step describe/?1/Report()                                         # `return { line: .., points: [r.score] }`
known #130 step describe/?1/Report()#2                            # what follows the early return is the other arm

line entry > describe call
line Fit | Failed·r > describe value # the route's parameter, by its name
known #130 line Fit | Failed·r > describe/?1/Report() value # `r.score`
known #130 line Fit | Failed·r > describe/?1/Report()#2 value # `r.reason`
known #130 line describe/?1/Report() > Report@describe/?1 value   # with the other arm's Report, the value either arm makes
known #130 line describe/?1/Report()#2 > Report@describe/?1 value
known #130 line Report@describe/?1 > describe value
line describe > Report@describe value                             # the result goes on to the caller

home Fit | Failed·r describe
known #130 home Report@describe/?1 describe
home Report@describe describe

side entry left

# the early return is read as a choice of one arm, and what follows it as a step after the choice
known #130 extra step describe/Report()
known #130 extra line describe/Report() > Report@describe/Report() value
known #130 extra line Report@describe/Report() > describe value
known #130 extra home Report@describe/Report() describe

# a library operation whose result no name holds and which changes nothing it runs on (`r.score.toFixed(2)`) stands as
# an occurrence, and what it gives as a value
known #125 extra step describe/?1/r.score.toFixed
known #125 extra line describe/?1/r.score.toFixed > _@describe/?1/r.score.toFixed value
known #125 extra line _@describe/?1/r.score.toFixed > describe/?1/Report() value
known #125 extra home _@describe/?1/r.score.toFixed describe/?1
known #130 extra line describe/?1/Report() > Report@describe/?1/Report() value
known #130 extra home Report@describe/?1/Report() describe/?1
known #125 extra line Fit | Failed·r > describe/?1/r.score.toFixed value # toFixed is no step
known #130 extra line Fit | Failed·r > describe/Report() value # the Report of the other arm of `?:`, which is no choice yet
